~ on_enter_bedroom
do freezePlayer()
if SaveLoad.SaveFileData.completed_house_tour:
#	do player.hide()
	do spawn_npc("res://resources/scenes/objects/NPCs/Cai.tscn", 125.0, 47.0)
	do player.global_position = Vector2(-18.0, 13.0)
	do player.reparent(get_npc("cai"))
	do changeCameraTarget(player)
	do camera.change_zoom(2.7)
	do get_npc("cai").movement_speed = 40.0
	do get_npc("cai").walk_to(Vector2(-75.0,-100.0))
	Cai: You can sleep alone?
	Cai: Good, good.

do unfreezePlayer()
=> END

~ insomina
do freezePlayer()
Queen: You have more energy still? I must admit it is admirable.
Queen: However, that does mean you will not be sleeping anytime soon unless you let some of it out.
Queen: ... Let's look around a bit, maybe you will find something illuminating about Cai. Unfortunately, she will not be going away anytime soon.
do unfreezePlayer()
=> END
~ necklace
*Inside the drawer are two necklaces. You pick them up, and something about it draws your gaze.*
#do animation_player.play("magnet")

*It's almost hypnotic in a way. To see the necklace complete.*

Speaking of complete, do you feel complete?
- Yes
	It would be nice to feel complete when everything is changing around you, when nothing seems to be stable or familiar.
	If you are lying to me, I cannot tell.
	For I am a necklace. 
- No
	That is fair it's all been moving so fast, hasn't it? Im sure you will find some time to slow down soon, but don't end up like me. 
	In some drawer, alone to gather dust. Maybe it wouldn't be so bad if I had another to spend that time with.
	But what would I know, I am but a necklace.
I have another question, if you will permit it.
Have you ever lost someone, someone who was as close as family, or maybe was?
- Yes
	I'm sorry to hear so. It's dreadfully common in this town. This town used to be thousands of souls bigger, and well. It isn't now, is it? 
	I can relate to that feeling. Of loss.
- No
	You're lucky, but not many others are. I haven't been able to see many others, but I know that loss is something many of us have in common. Try to sympathize; put yourself in their shoes.
- I don't have to tell a necklace about myself.
	WELL, it was more rhetorical anyway.

I'll tell you I used to be two, hanging on two people's necks all day long, and I would only be whole when they were close, they were so happy sometimes they would put one of me onto a smaller person who made me herself out of love. 
But one day they took me off, and never came back. It was a strange feeling because, despite being two, only one person wore me every day, all day, for a long time. I was whole. Yet, she was so sad. And she was for a long time.

I still don't think that I will ever get used to feeling whole like this, but I don't want to go back to being two anymore. 

Isn't that strange?

- Yes
	I'm glad you agree. After all, it would be strange to disagree with a necklace.  But the feeling will still stay no matter how I think I should feel.
- No
	Oh. I see. I guess you're right in a way. But the feeling will still stay no matter how I feel.

It may be rude for me to ask. But this talk of loss has got me wondering.
Do *you* have any family?
- Yes.
	Oh, do tell? I did see that taller person tuck you in, in a hurry. Would it be her?
	- She's my mom.
		Isn't that sweet. I think I remember the little one having one of those, my right half was mostly on a mom. 
	- She's my caretaker.
		A caretaker. That's very good to have at your age, I couldn't imagine what it's like to be deprived at one in a time of need. I would say things would go bad very, very fast. 
	- No. 
		I see. Well atleast you have someone around. After all it's not like your parents are here for you. Although that might be an insentive thing to say.
- No.
	=> nofamily
- Not anymore
	~ nofamily
	Im sorry for your loss, that really is quite sad. But. I wouldn't stop looking. Families are what you make of them. You don't have to be related. But I hope you find someone you may call a friend.

I'm glad we met, but I have one final question. Just between us?
Isn't it strange you're talking to something that can't talk.
- Yes
- No

Queen: What? I was lost in my thoughts since you were busy doing nothing. 
Queen: If you are done staring at that locket, I have been thinking about something for a long time, and I think now would be perfect. 
Queen: Down the road, just a short walk, is there a factory, inside the machinery is a room with a container and gauge. That gauge will tell us how long until their flamers' fuel runs dry.
Queen: Why don't you go find us a way to that factory? It is just left of the front of the building, a night walk, if you will.
Queen: Then maybe you will be able to sleep.
=> END